.TH echo 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
echo \- write arguments to standard output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B echo
[\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-e\fR] [\fIstring\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B echo
writes its arguments separated by spaces, followed by a newline.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Do not write the trailing newline.
.TP
.B \-e
Interpret backslash escapes in the arguments.
.PP
Options are only recognised before the first ordinary argument.
.SH ESCAPES
With
.BR \-e :
.B \\b
backspace,
.B \\f
formfeed,
.B \\n
newline,
.B \\r
carriage return,
.B \\t
tab,
.B \\v
vertical tab,
.B \\\\
backslash,
.B \\0\fInnn\fR
a byte by octal code, and
.B \\c
which stops output there and leaves off the newline.
.PP
Without
.BR \-e ,
backslashes are printed as they stand.
.SH NOTES
The shell has no
.B echo
built in, so this program runs even for a bare
.BR echo .
That makes it convenient but not free: each one is a fork and an exec.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR printenv (1),
.BR sh (1)
